# Top-level navigation for the documentation site.
#
# The order here is the order a new user should meet the app in: what it is,
# then the capture overlay, then the editor the capture lands in, then the
# settings that change both, then the reference material.
#
# `cli.md`, `cloud-accounts.md`, `releases.md` and `privacy.md` stay at the top
# level (and so keep their URLs). Each guide section is a folder with its own
# `.pages`.
#
# `releases.md` is generated at deploy time (scripts/gen-releases-page.py); the
# committed copy is a placeholder. It is listed here like any other page, so
# the nav entry is the same whichever copy is being built.
nav:
  - Home: index.md
  - getting-started.md
  - capture
  - editor
  - settings
  - Command line: cli.md
  - Cloud accounts: cloud-accounts.md
  - releases.md
  - privacy.md
  - terms.md
